    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d451">

                <pb facs="0536" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/147: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-11T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1927—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>87. Your 128, May 8, 4 p.m. The President approves President Diaz’s request and
                    Admiral Latimer will be instructed accordingly by the Navy Department.<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d451-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d451-f1" n="43" xml:id="d451-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Robert Rhea, on May 12, was appointed Chief of the Constabulary; and Col.
                    Elias R. Beadle, on August 20, was commissioned a general in command of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Guardia Nacional de Nicaragua</hi> (file Nos.
                    817.00/4775 and 817.1051/164).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
